==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|en-|throne}}; compare earlier {{m|en|enthronize}}, {{m|en|inthronize}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|əʊn|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|enthron}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To put on the [[throne]] in a formal installation ceremony called ''[[enthronement]]'', equivalent to (and often combined with) [[coronation]] and/or other ceremonies of [[investiture]]
# {{lb|en|transitive|figuratively}} To help a candidate to the succession of a monarchy (as a kingmaker does), or by extension in any other major organisation.

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|dethrone}}

